  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Applied Landscape Genetics to Chimpanzee Conservation in Guinea Bissau</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to work closely with Guinean counterparts to use genetic tools to determine demographic management units, corresponding to chimpanzee conservation needs in Guinea-Bissau and integrate the resulting genetic management plan into a national action plan for chimpanzees. The Recipient will assess the geographic distribution of genetic diversity of Pan troglodytes versus within Guinea-Bissau; assess anthropogenic barriers to dispersal; carry out a population viability assessment and propose specific actions for conservation, focusing on connectivity; and prepare the implementation of conservation actions.</narrative>
  </description>
